{"nodes": [{"id": "context_quantization_strategies", "label": "Inventaire des strat\u00e9gies de quantification (S4202, source de v\u00e9rit\u00e9)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/context/quantization_strategies.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_quantization_strategies_fp32", "label": "FP32 (r\u00e9f\u00e9rence)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/quantization_strategies.md", "source_location": "\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Format natif du Cortex-M4F (FPU), toujours la r\u00e9f\u00e9rence ; pi\u00e8ge : conclure d'un \u00e9chec INT8 que la quantification ne marche pas alors que le sch\u00e9ma (scale) compte, pas le principe (S39)."}, {"id": "context_quantization_strategies_int8_qat", "label": "INT8 QAT fake-quant PC (STE)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/quantization_strategies.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Le gradient voit l'erreur de quantification via straight-through estimator, donc m\u00e9trique pr\u00e9serv\u00e9e (\u0394\u22640,006 EWC) ; mais scales appris non export\u00e9s vers firmware \u2192 \u00e9cart QAT PC \u2705 / PTQ board \u274c du Sprint 36."}, {"id": "context_quantization_strategies_int8_ptq_legacy", "label": "INT8 PTQ legacy board (\u00e9chelle fig\u00e9e 1/128)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/quantization_strategies.md", "source_location": "\u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Destructeur (F1 0,96\u21920,07 pronostia) ; diagnostic S3904 : la cause dominante est l'\u00e9chelle fig\u00e9e non calibr\u00e9e, pas l'overflow int16 \u2014 per_tensor_calib r\u00e9cup\u00e8re tout (0,118\u21920,920). \u00c0 proscrire, conserv\u00e9 comme baseline p\u00e9dagogique."}, {"id": "context_quantization_strategies_int8_v2", "label": "INT8 v2 per-tensor/per-channel calibr\u00e9", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/quantization_strategies.md", "source_location": "\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PTQ calibr\u00e9e (round, acc int32, d\u00e9quant exacte FPU) : r\u00e9cup\u00e8re la m\u00e9trique FP32 en 8 bits, RAM \u00d74 ; validation board online S40 \u00ab \u00e0 mesurer \u00bb ; latence non am\u00e9lior\u00e9e sans noyau entier SIMD/CMSIS-NN."}, {"id": "context_quantization_strategies_q15", "label": "Q15 (grille 16 bits)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/quantization_strategies.md", "source_location": "\u00a75", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "65 536 niveaux, pas 258\u00d7 plus fin qu'INT8 : d\u00e9cisif pour tenseurs \u00e0 grande dynamique (sigma_inv_ Paderborn ~6,6e5, 11/25 coefficients \u00e9cras\u00e9s \u00e0 0 en INT8). AUROC r\u00e9cup\u00e9r\u00e9e (Pronostia \u22120,113\u2192+0,013), parit\u00e9 board exacte ; mu_ reste INT8 (piste future)."}, {"id": "context_quantization_strategies_int16_am", "label": "HDC int16-AM (m\u00e9moire associative int16)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/quantization_strategies.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pas une quantification par scale : r\u00e9tr\u00e9cissement du type d'accumulateur de classe avec SAT16, sans perte tant que les comptes ne saturent pas \u2014 \u0394=0 partout, RAM \u00d72,33."}, {"id": "context_quantization_strategies_latency_paradox", "label": "Paradoxe latence FPU (INT8 pas plus rapide)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/context/quantization_strategies.md", "source_location": "Limites", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": 